# [WIMSE](../wg/wimse.html)

## Summary

The WIMSE Interim meeting was held to receive updates on working group progress and discuss a proposed individual draft on the Workload Authorization Grant (WAG). 

Co-chairs Justin Richer and Pieter Kasselman opened the session with administrative updates and planning for IETF 121. The main technical presentation was delivered by Paul Carleton on "Workload Authorization Grant (WAG)", an individual draft co-authored with Nick Steele, Aaron Parecki, Arndt Schwenkschuster, and Brian Campbell. The working group discussed the scoping of the draft, its relationship to the active draft [draft-ietf-wimse-aims], potential extension profiles (e.g., for assistive and autonomous agents), and the path forward for adoption. An informal poll showed strong support for the problem space and the proposed document as a starting point.

